The Shrewd Dude schrieb:
> 
> Displaced Avenger wrote:
> > First of all, that ant's acting funny.  Soldier ants get two attacks
> > per round, and the *second* attack is poisoned.  This one got in six
> > attacks, or three rounds of two each, but the *first* attack of the
> > second round was poisoned.  That just ain't right.
> 
> It got in attacks because you were praying. Simple.

The objection is that the normal-version soldier ant has only two
attacks per round, one bite and one (poisoned) sting. A total of six
blows means it got in three rounds of attacks and performed a poisoned
attack in the wrong place.

[killed a unicorn with thrown daggers; corpse isn't in a cardinal
direction from player's current position]
> Ok, so I misplaced the corpse. But just assume that you moved onto the
> web.

What for? You're food-poisoned. Walking around is just a bad move in
that situation. Even #praying without being sure it's safe and _while
there's an uncursed unicorn horn just a few steps away_ is a very poor
move.

> > You can't win this scenario, because you either don't have enough
> > information, or it's impossible to get into this scenario in the first
> > place.
> 
> No, actually you can.

It's quite difficult to get into the situation described. Gaining the
"slow" intrinsic as a player might prove hardest.

> In fact, I'm posting the solution:
> 
> Whatever you do, the ant will get in one round of attacks.

Since you'll probably have normal speed if this happened in a game of
NetHack (and not some hacked variant), that doesn't follow. The ant's
faster, but not so much so that it will always get a free move.

To save one turn, i'd suggest switching on autopickup - make sure it's
set so that it picks up tools, but preferably not food.

